\": true, \"n_events_u_to_v\": 5, \"n_events_v_to_u\": 6, \"u\": 28, \"v\": 1141, \"window\": [0, 100000]}", "latency_ms": 0, "tokens_before": 18432, "tokens_after": 18432, "ok": true, "error": ""}], "final_claim": {"task_id": "t_2715f511", "decision": "insufficient", "mechanism": "cascade", "entities": [1085, 1141, 639], "window": [21277, 59677], "confidence": 0.6, "evidence": [{"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_04", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_05", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_06", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_07", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_09", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_10", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_08", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_11", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_12", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_14", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "The only candidate cascade is 1085->1141->639, supported by exactly one event on each leg and no direct 1085->639 edge. 1141 is a high-degree hub (303 events, 247 partners, 1030 triangles, tightly coupled to super-hub 28), so this static 2-hop link is well explained by hub mixing rather than influence transmission. Decisively, all available tools return only whole-horizon aggregates with no timestamps and no way to restrict to [21277, 59677]; I could verify neither the temporal ordering of the two legs nor the <=600-unit gap. Hence the temporal evidence needed to affirm or refute a time-respecting cascade is unavailable: insufficient."}, "raw_final_response": "**Findings**\n\n- Structural path exists but is razor thin: the only common node between 1085's out-neighbours (step_03) and 639's in-neighbours (step_04) is 1141, giving a single candidate 2-hop route 1085\u21921141\u2192639 (step_05, step_09).\n- That route rests on exactly one event per leg: 1085\u21921141 occurred once, 1141\u2192639 occurred once (step_06, step_07). There is no direct 1085\u2192639 edge at all (step_10).\n- Confounder checks: 1141 is a hub (303 events, 247 distinct partners, step_08; 4th most active node, step_12) sitting in 1030 triangles (step_11), and it is heavily coupled to the global super-hub 28 (step_14, step_13). So the static 2-hop connection is exactly what hub-mixing would produce by chance, and static reachability plus hub popularity are explicitly not sufficient grounds.\n- Critically, every tool in this session reports only whole-horizon aggregates ([0, 100000] windows); none of them exposed event timestamps or allowed restriction to [21277, 59677]. I therefore could not test either required temporal condition: (a) that the 1085\u21921141 event precedes the 1141\u2192639 event, or (b) that the gap between them is \u2264 600 time units. With single-shot legs there is a 50% prior that ordering alone fails, and the 600-unit gap constraint is a further, unverified restriction over a 38,400-unit interval.\n\nI decline to call this cascade \"present\" on structure alone, and I cannot call it \"absent\" without seeing the two timestamps.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_2715f511\",\n  \"decision\": \"insufficient\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1085, 1141, 639],\n  \"window\": [21277, 59677],\n  \"confidence\": 0.6,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"The only candidate cascade is 1085->1141->639, supported by exactly one event on each leg and no direct 1085->639 edge. 1141 is a high-degree hub (303 events, 247 partners, 1030 triangles, tightly coupled to super-hub 28), so this static 2-hop link is well explained by hub mixing rather than influence transmission. Decisively, all available tools return only whole-horizon aggregates with no timestamps and no way to restrict to [21277, 59677]; I could verify neither the temporal ordering of the two legs nor the <=600-unit gap. Hence the temporal evidence needed to affirm or refute a time-respecting cascade is unavailable: insufficient.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 24089, "total_output_tokens": 5689, "total_tokens": 29778, "total_latency_ms": 86404, "llm_calls": 6, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}